icRegression to a tree ensemble (RandomForest) to capture nonlinear interactions (e.g. Pclass×Sex, Fare bins). Hold features, split, seed fixed at 42. Expected runtime ~2s. If validation accuracy beats 0.8436, non-linearities add signal; otherwise LR with engineered features stays best. Writes both complete outputs.</goal>\n<code>import os, json, joblib, numpy as np, pandas as pd\nfrom sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\nfrom sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder\nfrom sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\nfrom sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\n\nseed = 42\nbase = "../input/data"\ntrain = pd.read_csv(f"{base}/train_data/train.csv")\nval = pd.read_csv(f"{base}/validation_data/validation.csv")\ntest = pd.read_csv(f"{base}/predict_data/test.csv")\n\ndef featurize(df):\n    d = df.copy()\n    d["FamilySize"] = d["SibSp"] + d["Parch"] + 1\n    d["IsAlone"] = (d["FamilySize"] == 1).astype(int)\n    title = d["Name"].str.extract(r",\\s*([^.]+)\\.", expand=False)\n    title = title.replace({"Mlle":"Miss","Ms":"Miss","Mme":"Mrs"})\n    rare = ~title.isin(["Mr","Mrs","Miss","Master"])\n    d["Title"] = np.where(rare, "Rare", title.fillna("Rare"))\n    return d\n\ntr_f, val_f, te_f = featurize(train), featurize(val), featurize(test)\nX_tr = tr_f.drop(columns=["Survived"]); y_tr = tr_f["Survived"].values\nval_ids = val_f["PassengerId"].tolist()\n\nnum_cols = ["Pclass", "SibSp", "Parch", "FamilySize", "IsAlone", "Age", "Fare"]\ncat_cols = ["Sex", "Embarked", "Title"]\n\npre = ColumnTransformer([\n    ("num", SimpleImputer(strategy="median"), num_cols),\n    ("cat", Pipeline([("imp", SimpleImputer(strategy="constant", fill_value="M")),\n                      ("oh", OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown="ignore"))]), cat_cols),\n])\nclf = Pipeline([("pre", pre),\n                ("rf", RandomForestClassifier(n_estimators=400, max_depth=6,\n                                              min_samples_leaf=3, random_state=seed,\n                                              n_jobs=4))])\nclf.fit(X_tr, y_tr)\n\nval_pred = (clf.predict_proba(val_f)[:, 1] >= 0.5).astype(int)\npd.DataFrame({"PassengerId": val_ids, "Survived": val_pred}).to_csv(\n    "work/val_predictions.csv", index=False)\n\ntest_pred = (clf.predict_proba(te_f)[:, 1] >= 0.5).astype(int)\npp = pd.DataFrame({"PassengerId": te_f["PassengerId"].values, "Survived": test_pred})\npp.to_csv("predictions.csv", index=False)\n\njson.dump({"model": "RandomForest + Title/FamilySize", "seed": seed,\n           "params": {"n_estimators":400,"max_depth":6,"min_samples_leaf":3}},\n          open("work/metrics.json", "w"), indent=2)\njoblib.dump(clf, "work/model_rf.joblib")\nopen("work/README.txt", "w").write(\n    "Inference: load model_rf.joblib; predict_proba[:,1] >= 0.5 -> 1.\\n"\n    "RandomForest(400, depth 6) on engineered features. Seed 42, CPU, n_jobs=4.")\n\nvp = pd.read_csv("work/val_predictions.csv")\nassert vp["PassengerId"].tolist() == val_ids and len(vp) == 179\nassert len(pp) == 418 and pp["PassengerId"].tolist() == te_f["PassengerId"].tolist()\nassert set(pp["Survived"].unique()) <= {0, 1}\nprint("val rows", len(vp), "test rows", len(pp), "test pos rate", pp["Survived"].mean().round(3))\n</code>\n<validation_prediction_file>work/val_predictions.csv</validation_prediction_file>\n<prediction_file>predictions.csv</prediction_file>'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Execution time: 4.07 seconds; success: True.\n<output>val rows 179 test rows 418 test pos rate 0.364</output>\n<error></error>\nUse this evidence to repair failures or test the next controlled improvement.\n\nMeasured fixed-split validation metric: Metric↑(0.8324). Best so far: Metric↑(0.8436).\n\nRespond with exactly one executable notebook cell, using these tags:\n<goal>Hypothesis, expected runtime, expected output and how it tests the hypothesis</goal>\n<code>Python code for the next cell, without Markdown fences</code>\n<validation_prediction_file>Relative file path for complete validation predictions, or None</validation_prediction_file>\n<prediction_file>Relative file path for complete business prediction output, or None</prediction_file>\nBoth file tags must be None unless this cell writes BOTH complete outputs.\nDo not report an estimated score: the independent local evaluator measures it.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': '<goal>RandomForest (0.8324) underperformed LR with engineered features (0.8436). Revert to the best LR pipeline but add one more controlled feature: a binned Fare feature (FareBin via qcut into quantiles) plus log(Fare+1), since fare is skewed and interacts with class. Keep everything else (features, split, seed, LR) identical to the best run. Expected runtime ~1s. If validation accuracy exceeds 0.8436, fare binning helps; otherwise I roll back to the best model. Writes both complete outputs.</goal>\n<code>import os, json, joblib, numpy as np, pandas as pd\nfrom sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\nfrom sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder\nfrom sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n\nseed = 42\nbase = "../input/data"\ntrain = pd.read_csv(f"{base}/train_data/train.csv")\nval = pd.read_csv(f"{base}/validation_data/validation.csv")\ntest = pd.read_csv(f"{base}/predict_data/test.csv")\n\ndef featurize(df):\n    d = df.copy()\n    d["FamilySize"] = d["SibSp"] + d["Parch"] + 1\n    d["IsAlone"] = (d["FamilySize"] == 1).astype(int)\n    title = d["Name"].str.extract(r",\\s*([^.]+)\\.", expand=False)\n    title = title.replace({"Mlle":"Miss","Ms":"Miss","Mme":"Mrs"})\n    rare = ~title.isin(["Mr","Mrs","Miss","Master"])\n    d["Title"] = np.where(rare, "Rare", title.fillna("Rare"))\n    d["LogFare"] = np.log1p(d["Fare"].fillna(d["Fare"].median()))\n    return d\n\ntr_f, val_f, te_f = featurize(train), featurize(val), featurize(test)\nX_tr = tr_f.drop(columns=["Survived"]); y_tr = tr_f["Survived"].values\nval_ids = val_f["PassengerId"].tolist()\n\nnum_cols = ["Pclass", "SibSp", "Parch", "FamilySize", "IsAlone", "LogFare"]\naf_cols = ["Age", "Fare"]\ncat_cols = ["Sex", "Embarked", "Title"]\n\npre = ColumnTransformer([\n    ("num", SimpleImputer(strategy="median"), num_cols),\n    ("af", SimpleImputer(strategy="median", add_indicator=True), af_cols),\n    ("cat", Pipeline([("imp", SimpleImputer(strategy="constant", fill_value="M")),\n                      ("oh", OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown="ignore"))]), cat_cols),\n])\nclf = Pipeline([("pre", pre),\n                ("lr", LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000, random_state=seed))])\nclf.fit(X_tr, y_tr)\n\nval_pred = (clf.predict_proba(val_f)[:, 1] >= 0.5).astype(int)\npd.DataFrame({"PassengerId": val_ids, "Survived": val_pred}).to_csv(\n    "work/val_predictions.csv", index=False)\n\ntest_pred = (clf.predict_proba(te_f)[:, 1] >= 0.5).astype(int)\npp = pd.DataFrame({"PassengerId": te_f["PassengerId"].values, "Survived": test_pred})\npp.to_csv("predictions.csv", index=False)\n\njson.dump({"model": "LogisticRegression + Title/FamilySize/IsAlone/LogFare", "seed": seed},\n          open("work/metrics.json", "w"), indent=2)\njoblib.dump(clf, "work/model_fe2.joblib")\nopen("work/README.txt", "w").write(\n    "Inference: load model_fe2.joblib; predict_proba[:,1] >= 0.5 -> 1.\\n"\n    "LR on Pclass,SibSp,Parch,FamilySize,IsAlone,LogFare numeric; Age/Fare median+indicator; "\n    "Sex/Embarked(missing->\'M\')/Title one-hot. Seed 42, CPU only.")\n\nvp = pd.read_csv("work/val_predictions.csv")\nassert vp["PassengerId"].tolist() == val_ids and len(vp) == 179\nassert len(pp) == 418 and pp["PassengerId"].tolist() == te_f["PassengerId"].tolist()\nassert set(pp["Survived"].unique()) <= {0, 1}\nprint("val rows", len(vp), "test rows", len(pp), "test pos rate", pp["Survived"].mean().round(3))\n</code>\n<validation_prediction_file>work/val_predictions.csv</validation_prediction_file>\n<prediction_file>predictions.csv</prediction_file>'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Execution time: 0.07 seconds; success: True.\n<output>val rows 179 test rows 418 test pos rate 0.392</output>\n<error></error>\nUse this evidence to repair failures or test the next controlled improvement.\n\nMeasured fixed-split validation metric: Metric↑(0.8324). Best so far: Metric↑(0.8436).\n\nRespond with exactly one executable notebook cell, using these tags:\n<goal>Hypothesis, expected runtime, expected output and how it tests the hypothesis</goal>\n<code>Python code for the next cell, without Markdown fences</code>\n<validation_prediction_file>Relative file path for complete validation predictions, or None</validation_prediction_file>\n<prediction_file>Relative file path for complete business prediction output, or None</prediction_file>\nBoth file tags must be None unless this cell writes BOTH complete outputs.\nDo not report an estimated score: the independent local evaluator measures it.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': '<goal>LogFare (0.8324) hurt vs the best (0.8436), so drop it. Best so far was LR with Title+FamilySize+IsAlone and raw Age/Fare. Now make one controlled regularization change on that exact feature set: add class_weight=\'balanced\' to handle the 62/38 imbalance, keeping features, seed, and split identical. Expected runtime ~1s. If accuracy exceeds 0.8436, class weighting helps; otherwise I restore the exact best model. Writes both complete outputs.</goal>\n<code>import os, json, joblib, numpy as np, pandas as pd\nfrom sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\nfrom sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder\nfrom sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n\nseed = 42\nbase = "../input/data"\ntrain = pd.read_csv(f"{base}/train_data/train.csv")\nval = pd.read_csv(f"{base}/validation_data/validation.csv")\ntest = pd.read_csv(f"{base}/predict_data/test.csv")\n\ndef featurize(df):\n    d = df.copy()\n    d["FamilySize"] = d["SibSp"] + d["Parch"] + 1\n    d["IsAlone"] = (d["FamilySize"] == 1).astype(int)\n    title = d["Name"].str.extract(r",\\s*([^.]+)\\.", expand=False)\n    title = title.replace({"Mlle":"Miss","Ms":"Miss","Mme":"Mrs"})\n    rare = ~title.isin(["Mr","Mrs","Miss","Master"])\n    d["Title"] = np.where(rare, "Rare", title.fillna("Rare"))\n    return d\n\ntr_f, val_f, te_f = featurize(train), featurize(val), featurize(test)\nX_tr = tr_f.drop(columns=["Survived"]); y_tr = tr_f["Survived"].values\nval_ids = val_f["PassengerId"].tolist()\n\nnum_cols = ["Pclass", "SibSp", "Parch", "FamilySize", "IsAlone"]\naf_cols = ["Age", "Fare"]\ncat_cols = ["Sex", "Embarked", "Title"]\n\npre = ColumnTransformer([\n    ("num", SimpleImputer(strategy="median"), num_cols),\n    ("af", SimpleImputer(strategy="median", add_indicator=True), af_cols),\n    ("cat", Pipeline([("imp", SimpleImputer(strategy="constant", fill_value="M")),\n                      ("oh", OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown="ignore"))]), cat_cols),\n])\nclf = Pipeline([("pre", pre),\n                ("lr", LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000, random_state=seed,\n                                          class_weight="balanced"))])\nclf.fit(X_tr, y_tr)\n\nval_pred = (clf.predict_proba(val_f)[:, 1] >= 0.5).astype(int)\npd.DataFrame({"PassengerId": val_ids, "Survived": val_pred}).to_csv(\n    "work/val_predictions.csv", index=False)\n\ntest_pred = (clf.predict_proba(te_f)[:, 1] >= 0.5).astype(int)\npp = pd.DataFrame({"PassengerId": te_f["PassengerId"].values, "Survived": test_pred})\npp.to_csv("predictions.csv", index=False)\n\njson.dump({"model": "LR + Title/FamilySize/IsAlone, class_weight=balanced", "seed": seed},\n          open("work/metrics.json", "w"), indent=2)\njoblib.dump(clf, "work/model_cw.joblib")\nopen("work/README.txt", "w").write(\n    "Inference: load model_cw.joblib; predict_proba[:,1] >= 0.5 -> 1.\\n"\n    "LR(class_weight=balanced) on Pclass,SibSp,Parch,FamilySize,IsAlone numeric; "\n    "Age/Fare median+indicator; Sex/Embarked(missing->\'M\')/Title one-hot. Seed 42, CPU only.")\n\nvp = pd.read_csv("work/val_predictions.csv")\nassert vp["PassengerId"].tolist() == val_ids and len(vp) == 179\nassert len(pp) == 418 and pp["PassengerId"].tolist() == te_f["PassengerId"].tolist()\nassert set(pp["Survived"].unique()) <= {0, 1}\nprint("val rows", len(vp), "test rows", len(pp), "test pos rate", pp["Survived"].mean().round(3))\n</code>\n<validation_prediction_file>work/val_predictions.csv</validation_prediction_file>\n<prediction_file>predictions.csv</prediction_file>'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Execution time: 0.05 seconds; success: True.\n<output>val rows 179 test rows 418 test pos rate 0.435</output>\n<error></error>\nUse this evidence to repair failures or test the next controlled improvement.\n\nMeasured fixed-split validation metric: Metric↑(0.8268). Best so far: Metric↑(0.8436).\n\nRespond with exactly one executable notebook cell, using these tags:\n<goal>Hypothesis, expected runtime, expected output and how it tests the hypothesis</goal>\n<code>Python code for the next cell, without Markdown fences</code>\n<validation_prediction_file>Relative file path for complete validation predictions, or None</validation_prediction_file>\n<prediction_file>Relative file path for complete business prediction output, or None</prediction_file>\nBoth file tags must be None unless this cell writes BOTH complete outputs.\nDo not report an estimated score: the independent local evaluator measures it.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': '<goal>Class weighting (0.8268) hurt, so revert to the exact best config (LR + Title/FamilySize/IsAlone, no weighting → 0.8436). Now make one controlled addition: also one-hot Pclass as categorical alongside the numeric term would duplicate — instead, try a modest C regularization sweep on the same best feature set, picking C by a small internal 5-fold CV on the 712 training rows (never touching validation labels). Expected runtime ~3s. If a tuned C beats default, adopt it; otherwise keep C=1.0 best. Writes both complete outputs using the chosen model.</goal>\n<code>import os, json, joblib, numpy as np, pandas as pd\nfrom sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\nfrom sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder\nfrom sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import cross_val_score, StratifiedKFold\n\nseed = 42\nbase = "../input/data"\ntrain = pd.read_csv(f"{base}/train_data/train.csv")\nval = pd.read_csv(f"{base}/validation_data/validation.csv")\ntest = pd.read_csv(f"{base}/predict_data/test.csv")\n\ndef featurize(df):\n    d = df.copy()\n    d["FamilySize"] = d["SibSp"] + d["Parch"] + 1\n    d["IsAlone"] = (d["FamilySize"] == 1).astype(int)\n    title = d["Name"].str.extract(r",\\s*([^.]+)\\.", expand=False)\n    title = title.replace({"Mlle":"Miss","Ms":"Miss","Mme":"Mrs"})\n    rare = ~title.isin(["Mr","Mrs","Miss","Master"])\n    d["Title"] = np.where(rare, "Rare", title.fillna("Rare"))\n    return d\n\ntr_f, val_f, te_f = featurize(train), featurize(val), featurize(test)\nX_tr = tr_f.drop(columns=["Survived"]); y_tr = tr_f["Survived"].values\nval_ids = val_f["PassengerId"].tolist()\n\nnum_cols = ["Pclass", "SibSp", "Parch", "FamilySize", "IsAlone"]\naf_cols = ["Age", "Fare"]\ncat_cols = ["Sex", "Embarked", "Title"]\n\ndef make_pipeline(C):\n    pre = ColumnTransformer([\n        ("num", SimpleImputer(strategy="median"), num_cols),\n        ("af", SimpleImputer(strategy="median", add_indicator=True), af_cols),\n        ("cat", Pipeline([("imp", SimpleImputer(strategy="constant", fill_value="M")),\n                          ("oh", OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown="ignore"))]), cat_cols),\n    ])\n    return Pipeline([("pre", pre),\n                     ("lr", LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000, random_state=seed, C=C))])\n\ncv = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=seed)\nbest_C, best_cv = 1.0, -1\nfor C in [0.03, 0.1, 0.3, 1.0, 3.0, 10.0]:\n    s = cross_val_score(make_pipeline(C), X_tr, y_tr, cv=cv,\n                        scoring="accuracy", n_jobs=1).mean()\n    print(f"C={C:<5} cv_acc={s:.4f}")\n    if s > best_cv:\n        best_cv, best_C = s, C\nprint("chosen C:", best_C, "cv:", round(best_cv,4))\n\nclf = make_pipeline(best_C)\nclf.fit(X_tr, y_tr)\n\nval_pred = (clf.predict_proba(val_f)[:, 1] >= 0.5).astype(int)\npd.DataFrame({"PassengerId": val_ids, "Survived": val_pred}).to_csv(\n    "work/val_predictions.csv", index=False)\n\ntest_pred = (clf.predict_proba(te_f)[:, 1] >= 0.5).astype(int)\npp = pd.DataFrame({"PassengerId": te_f["PassengerId"].values, "Survived": test_pred})\npp.to_csv("predictions.csv", index=False)\n\njson.dump({"model": "LR + Title/FamilySize/IsAlone, tuned C", "seed": seed,\n           "C": best_C, "cv_acc": best_cv}, open("work/metrics.json", "w"), indent=2)\njoblib.dump(clf, "work/model_best.joblib")\nopen("work/README.txt", "w").write(\n    f"Inference: load model_best.joblib (C={best_C}); predict_proba[:,1] >= 0.5 -> 1.\\n"\n    "LR on Pclass,SibSp,Parch,FamilySize,IsAlone numeric; Age/Fare median+indicator; "\n    "Sex/Embarked(missing->\'M\')/Title one-hot. C chosen by 5-fold CV on train only. Seed 42, CPU.")\n\nvp = pd.read_csv("work/val_predictions.csv")\nassert vp["PassengerId"].tolist() == val_ids and len(vp) == 179\nassert len(pp) == 418 and pp["PassengerId"].tolist() == te_f["PassengerId"].tolist()\nassert set(pp["Survived"].unique()) <= {0, 1}\nprint("val rows", len(vp), "test rows", len(pp), "test pos rate", pp["Survived"].mean().round(3))\n</code>\n<validation_prediction_file>work/val_predictions.csv</validation_prediction_file>\n<prediction_file>predictions.csv</prediction_file>'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Execution time: 0.70 seconds; success: True.\n<output>C=0.03  cv_acc=0.8132\nC=0.1   cv_acc=0.8188\nC=0.3   cv_acc=0.8202\nC=1.0   cv_acc=0.8203\nC=3.0   cv_acc=0.8189\nC=10.0  cv_acc=0.8174\nchosen C: 1.0 cv: 0.8203