al cell is a no-op confirmation that re-states the chosen deliverables and metrics from disk (no model change, no new writes beyond re-affirming schema), so the round ends cleanly with the best-measured configuration in place.</goal>\n<code>import json, pandas as pd\n# Confirmation only: no model change. Re-affirm on-disk deliverables.\nvp = pd.read_csv("work/val_predictions.csv")\npp = pd.read_csv("predictions.csv")\nassert list(pp.columns) == ["PassengerId","Survived"] and len(pp) == 418\nassert list(vp.columns) == ["PassengerId","Survived"] and len(vp) == 179\nassert set(pp["Survived"].unique()) <= {0,1}\nsummary = {\n    "status": "complete",\n    "best_model": "LogisticRegression + Title/FamilySize/IsAlone (scaled, Age/Fare median+indicator)",\n    "seed": 42,\n    "val_prediction_file": "work/val_predictions.csv",\n    "business_prediction_file": "predictions.csv",\n    "val_rows": len(vp),\n    "test_rows": len(pp),\n    "note": "No further single-factor improvement exceeded the best measured validation accuracy; best configuration retained.",\n}\nprint(json.dumps(summary, indent=2))\n</code>\n<validation_prediction_file>work/val_predictions.csv</validation_prediction_file>\n<prediction_file>predictions.csv</prediction_file>'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Execution time: 0.01 seconds; success: True.\n<output>{\n  "status": "complete",\n  "best_model": "LogisticRegression + Title/FamilySize/IsAlone (scaled, Age/Fare median+indicator)",\n  "seed": 42,\n  "val_prediction_file": "work/val_predictions.csv",\n  "business_prediction_file": "predictions.csv",\n  "val_rows": 179,\n  "test_rows": 418,\n  "note": "No further single-factor improvement exceeded the best measured validation accuracy; best configuration retained."\n}</output>\n<error></error>\nUse this evidence to repair failures or test the next controlled improvement.\n\nMeasured fixed-split validation metric: Metric↑(0.8436). Best so far: Metric↑(0.8436).\n\nRespond with exactly one executable notebook cell, using these tags:\n<goal>Hypothesis, expected runtime, expected output and how it tests the hypothesis</goal>\n<code>Python code for the next cell, without Markdown fences</code>\n<validation_prediction_file>Relative file path for complete validation predictions, or None</validation_prediction_file>\n<prediction_file>Relative file path for complete business prediction output, or None</prediction_file>\nBoth file tags must be None unless this cell writes BOTH complete outputs.\nDo not report an estimated score: the independent local evaluator measures it.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'The best measured configuration (0.8436) is in place and stable. One remaining untested, low-risk single factor: a GridSearch-free, small internal-CV comparison of LR vs LinearSVC-style decision boundary is unlikely to help; instead the most promising untried controlled factor is adding an Age×Pclass or binned-Age interaction via a binned Age categorical, which can capture the known non-linear age-survival relationship while keeping the model linear. I\'ll try exactly that one change.\n\n<goal>Best model is LR + Title/FamilySize/IsAlone (0.8436). Test one new controlled feature addition on that exact model: an AgeBin categorical (child/teen/adult/senior via fixed thresholds fit deterministically), which lets LR capture the non-linear age-survival relationship without a nonlinear model. All other features, split, seed, scaling, and thresholds fixed. Expected runtime ~1s. If validation accuracy exceeds 0.8436, AgeBin adds signal; otherwise revert to prior best. Writes both complete outputs.</goal>\n<code>import os, json, joblib, numpy as np, pandas as pd, warnings\nfrom sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\nfrom sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder, StandardScaler\nfrom sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\nwarnings.filterwarnings("ignore")\n\nseed = 42\nbase = "../input/data"\ntrain = pd.read_csv(f"{base}/train_data/train.csv")\nval = pd.read_csv(f"{base}/validation_data/validation.csv")\ntest = pd.read_csv(f"{base}/predict_data/test.csv")\n\ndef featurize(df):\n    d = df.copy()\n    d["FamilySize"] = d["SibSp"] + d["Parch"] + 1\n    d["IsAlone"] = (d["FamilySize"] == 1).astype(int)\n    title = d["Name"].str.extract(r",\\s*([^.]+)\\.", expand=False)\n    title = title.replace({"Mlle":"Miss","Ms":"Miss","Mme":"Mrs"})\n    rare = ~title.isin(["Mr","Mrs","Miss","Master"])\n    d["Title"] = np.where(rare, "Rare", title.fillna("Rare"))\n    age = d["Age"]\n    d["AgeBin"] = pd.cut(age, bins=[-1, 12, 18, 60, 200],\n                         labels=["child","teen","adult","senior"]).astype(str)\n    d.loc[age.isna(), "AgeBin"] = "unknown"\n    return d\n\ntr_f, val_f, te_f = featurize(train), featurize(val), featurize(test)\nX_tr = tr_f.drop(columns=["Survived"]); y_tr = tr_f["Survived"].values\nval_ids = val_f["PassengerId"].tolist()\n\nnum_cols = ["Pclass", "SibSp", "Parch", "FamilySize", "IsAlone"]\naf_cols = ["Age", "Fare"]\ncat_cols = ["Sex", "Embarked", "Title", "AgeBin"]\n\npre = ColumnTransformer([\n    ("num", Pipeline([("imp", SimpleImputer(strategy="median")), ("sc", StandardScaler())]), num_cols),\n    ("af", Pipeline([("imp", SimpleImputer(strategy="median", add_indicator=True)), ("sc", StandardScaler())]), af_cols),\n    ("cat", Pipeline([("imp", SimpleImputer(strategy="constant", fill_value="M")),\n                      ("oh", OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown="ignore"))]), cat_cols),\n])\nclf = Pipeline([("pre", pre), ("lr", LogisticRegression(max_iter=2000, random_state=seed))])\nclf.fit(X_tr, y_tr)\n\nval_pred = (clf.predict_proba(val_f)[:, 1] >= 0.5).astype(int)\npd.DataFrame({"PassengerId": val_ids, "Survived": val_pred}).to_csv(\n    "work/val_predictions.csv", index=False)\n\ntest_pred = (clf.predict_proba(te_f)[:, 1] >= 0.5).astype(int)\npp = pd.DataFrame({"PassengerId": te_f["PassengerId"].values, "Survived": test_pred})\